        "description": "<p>Papy3D Menu Visibility allows administrators to control the visibility of navigation menu items based on WordPress capabilities.</p>\n<p>Features:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>Capability-based visibility</li>\n<li>Show or hide mode</li>\n<li>Full Site Editing support</li>\n<li>Accessibility-friendly admin UI</li>\n<li>Multisite-safe uninstall</li>\n<li>WordPress coding standards compliant</li>\n</ul>\n",
        "installation": "<ol>\n<li>Upload the plugin folder to <code>/wp-content/plugins/</code></li>\n<li>Activate the plugin through the WordPress admin</li>\n<li>Go to Appearance &gt; Menus</li>\n<li>Configure visibility settings for each menu item</li>\n</ol>\n",
        "changelog": "<p>= 1.1.1=<br />\n* Fix : Updated link Header<br />\n* Validated up to : 7.0</p>\n<h4>1.1.0</h4>\n<ul>\n<li>Full rewrite for WordPress 2026 standards</li>\n</ul>\n"
